Ordered lock codec third-party notices
=====================================

This private codec derives scalar parser/generator behavior from Ruby JSON
2.21.2 (https://github.com/ruby/json; C extension author Florian Frank as
identified by its json.gemspec). For those translations we select the complete
2-clause BSDL supplied through COPYING and LEGAL, reproduced below.

ordered_lock_float.go ports the bundled night-shift/fpconv implementation
(https://github.com/night-shift/fpconv), including Ruby JSON's modification
to append .0 to plain floats. Its complete embedded Boost1.0 notice follows.
The gem LEGAL names fpconv.h; the actual supplied and ported file is fpconv.c.
No SIMD/SWAR excerpt, fast_float, jeaiii, Ruby dtoa or Go internal source is
copied. Remaining validated numeric conversion calls public strconv.ParseFloat.

